al Resources."},"number":"HR 8006","policyArea":"Water Resources Development","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Amends Public Law 89-108 to authorize additional appropriations for water supply projects in North Dakota and tribal Indian reservations, including Northwest Area Water Supply, Eastern North Dakota Alternate Water Supply, Southwest Pipeline, and rural water systems for the Spirit Lake, Three Affiliated Tribes, Standing Rock, and Turtle Mountain Indian Reservations.","summarySource":"ai","title":"Dakota Water Resources Act Amendments of 2026","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/8006"},{"bipartisan":true,"cosponsors":1,"crossPartyCosponsors":1,"id":"hr7956-119","introducedDate":"2026-03-17","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2026-03-17","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Energy and Commerce."},"number":"HR 7956","policyArea":"Health","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Amends the Public Health Service Act to reauthorize the State Offices of Rural Health program by authorizing appropriations of $12.5 million annually through fiscal year 2027 and $13.5 million annually through fiscal year 2032.","summarySource":"ai","title":"State Offices of Rural Health Program Reauthorization Act of 2026","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/7956"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":4,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr6633-119","introducedDate":"2025-12-11","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2026-09-16","text":"Received in the Senate and Read twice and referred to the Committee on Energy and Natural Resources."},"number":"HR 6633","policyArea":"Energy","ranked":true,"stage":"passed_one_chamber","summary":"High-Capacity Grid Act This bill requires public electric utilities to use the best-available transmission conductor for certain interstate transmission lines (i.e., power lines) in order to recover the costs of the conductor through consumers' electric bills. Specifically, in any filing seeking to recover the costs of a transmission conductor for the transmission line and in any proceeding to...","summarySource":"crs","title":"High-Capacity Grid Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/6633"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":7,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr6336-119","introducedDate":"2025-12-01","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-12-01","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Energy and Commerce."},"number":"HR 6336","policyArea":"Energy","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Prohibits transmission providers from allocating costs for transmission facilities built to implement a state's policy to consumers in other states, unless those states expressly consent to cost allocation.","summarySource":"ai","title":"Fair Allocation of Interstate Rates Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/6336"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":0,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr5311-119","introducedDate":"2025-09-11","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-09-11","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Energy and Commerce."},"number":"HR 5311","policyArea":"Science, Technology, Communications","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Amends the Communications Act of 1934 to establish timelines and procedural requirements for cable franchising authorities' decisions on placement, construction, and modification of cable service facilities, while preserving their regulatory authority over such decisions.","summarySource":"ai","title":"CABLE Expansion Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/5311"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":0,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hjres105-119","introducedDate":"2025-07-10","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-12-11","text":"Became Public Law No: 119-49."},"number":"HJRES 105","policyArea":"Public Lands and Natural Resources","ranked":true,"stage":"became_law","summary":"This joint resolution nullifies the rule submitted by the Bureau of Land Management (BLM) relating to the Record of Decision and Approved Resource Management Plan (RMP) for the North Dakota Field Office and issued on January 8, 2025. By way of background, an RMP guides the management of lands administered by BLM. The 2025 North Dakota RMP modified the 1988 RMP, including by limiting development...","summarySource":"crs","title":"Providing for congressional disapproval under chapter 8 of title 5, United States Code, of the rule submitted by the Bureau of Land Management relating to \"North Dakota Field Office Record of Decision and Approved Resource Management Plan\".","type":"hjres","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-joint-resolution/105"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":26,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr3843-119","introducedDate":"2025-06-09","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-06-09","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Energy and Commerce."},"number":"HR 3843","policyArea":"Energy","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Amends the Federal Power Act to prohibit retirement or fuel conversion of baseload electric generating units in areas designated by the North American Electric Reliability Corporation as at high or elevated risk of electricity supply shortfalls, with limited exemptions available through Federal Energy Regulatory Commission petition and potential Department of Energy grants or loans.","summarySource":"ai","title":"Baseload Reliability Protection Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/3843"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":2,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr3062-119","introducedDate":"2025-04-29","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-09-19","text":"Received in the Senate and Read twice and referred to the Committee on Energy and Natural Resources."},"number":"HR 3062","policyArea":"Energy","ranked":true,"stage":"passed_one_chamber","summary":"Promoting Cross-b order Energy Infrastructure Act This bill establishes a new process for approving or revoking permits for the construction and operation of energy infrastructure across an international border of the United States. Thus, it replaces the existing process established under specified executive orders. The bill requires a person to obtain a certificate of crossing before...","summarySource":"crs","title":"Promoting Cross-border Energy Infrastructure Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/3062"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":4,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr2838-119","introducedDate":"2025-04-10","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-04-10","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Ways and Means."},"number":"HR 2838","policyArea":"Taxation","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Ending Intermittent Energy Subsidies Act of 2025 This bill phases out and eliminates the ability to transfer federal tax credits for solar and wind investments and energy production. Specifically, the bill phases out over five years the (1) clean electricity investment tax credit for investments in a facility that generates electricity using solar or wind energy, and (2) clean electricity...","summarySource":"crs","title":"Ending Intermittent Energy Subsidies Act of 2025","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/2838"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":1,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hres290-119","introducedDate":"2025-04-02","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-04-02","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Energy and Commerce."},"number":"HRES 290","policyArea":"Energy","ranked":false,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Recognizes that retirement of nonintermittent electric generation facilities before replacement with facilities having equal reliability attributes threatens U.S. electric grid reliability, and expresses concern about environmental regulations and federal incentives driving premature plant retirements.","summarySource":"ai","title":"Recognizing that the retirement of nonintermittent electric generation facilities, before facilities with equal or greater reliability attributes are available, is a threat to the reliability of the United States electric grid.","type":"hres","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-resolution/290"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":3,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hjres79-119","introducedDate":"2025-03-24","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-03-27","text":"Sponsor introductory remarks on measure. (CR H1328-1329)"},"number":"HJRES 79","policyArea":"Environmental Protection","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"This joint resolution nullifies the Environmental Protection Agency final rule titled Review of Final Rule Reclassification of Major Sources as Area Sources Under Section 112 of the Clean Air Act (89 Fed. Reg. 73293) and published on September 10, 2024. Among other elements, the rule requires sources of persistent and bioaccumulative hazardous air pollutants to continue to comply with certain...","summarySource":"crs","title":"Providing for congressional disapproval under chapter 8 of title 5, United States Code, of the rule submitted by the Environmental Protection Agency relating to \"Review of Final Rule Reclassification of Major Sources as Area Sources Under Section 112 of the Clean Air Act\".","type":"hjres","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-joint-resolution/79"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":0,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr2252-119","introducedDate":"2025-03-21","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2026-05-20","text":"Received in the Senate and Read twice and referred to the Committee on Energy and Natural Resources."},"number":"HR 2252","policyArea":"Public Lands and Natural Resources","ranked":true,"stage":"passed_one_chamber","summary":"North Dakota Trust Lands Completion Act of 2026 This bill allows North Dakota to exchange certain state land grant parcels (e.g., lands granted to North Dakota by Congress when it became a state) located wholly or partially within an Indian reservation for certain federal land of substantially equivalent value. North Dakota manages oil, gas, and agriculture leases on state land grant parcels to...","summarySource":"crs","title":"North Dakota Trust Lands Completion Act of 2026","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/2252"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":0,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr1830-119","introducedDate":"2025-03-04","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2026-09-14","text":"Placed on Senate Legislative Calendar under General Orders. Calendar No. 597."},"number":"HR 1830","policyArea":"Government Operations and Politics","ranked":true,"stage":"passed_one_chamber","summary":"This bill designates the facility of the United States Postal Service located at 840 Front Street in Casselton, North Dakota, as the \"Commander Delbert Austin Olson Post Office\".","summarySource":"crs","title":"To designate the facility of the United States Postal Service located at 840 Front Street in Casselton, North Dakota, as the \"Commander Delbert Austin Olson Post Office\".","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/1830"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":0,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hres32-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-13","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-13","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Education and Workforce."},"number":"HRES 32","policyArea":"Sports and Recreation","ranked":false,"stage":"introduced","summary":"This resolution congratulates the North Dakota State University Bison football team for winning the 2024 National Collegiate Athletic Association Division I Football Championship Subdivision title.","summarySource":"crs","title":"Congratulating the North Dakota State University Bison football team for winning the 2024 National Collegiate Athletic Association Division I Football Championship Subdivision title.","type":"hres","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bi